From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yewsifofficial <yewsifofficial@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:50:20 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] net: the console's socket numbers where they still differed,
 and a trace of the match attempt

Seeing arenas needs only the TCP connection; joining one or Quickplay needs
Pia's UDP as well, and that part has never been seen working here. Read
against the three clients that do it (SM35 Recomp, Nextendo's own Ryujinx
build, and WindowSmash for this very game), these still differed:

- Fcntl F_GETFL answered the non-blocking bit as FreeBSD's 4. The console's
  library has it at 0x800, as all three answer; SM35 Recomp lists it among
  the fixes on its way to a played match. The socket type takes the bit in
  either numbering too.
- Socket options went to the host socket by number. Horizon's numbers are
  FreeBSD's and Apple's agree only for the classic set (0x800 is SO_NOSIGPIPE
  there and a timestamp option here; IP option 65 is IP_RECVTTL there and a
  background traffic class here). Only the options whose number and meaning
  agree reach the host now, the ones SM35 Recomp passes on; the others are
  kept and read back as set, as Nextendo's Ryujinx build does.
- Names: nintendo.com, nintendo.co.jp and nintendowifi.net resolve to
  Nextendo too, as their Ryujinx build redirects them.

What a failed match attempt leaves in the log (DM_NEXTENDO_LOG=1):

- each NEX call across the bridge by protocol and method number, a failed
  call's result code, what the game reports of its NAT (ReportNATProperties)
  and of each hole punch. Numbers only: no station URL, token, name or id.
- every datagram socket's totals at its close, whatever the trace budget.
- every failure the game records in an nn::err::ErrorResultVariant, read on
  its way into the SDK's own function, which still does the work.
- observation gate OBS_PIA_FAIL on Pia's "this job failed" (main+0xb41f0 in
  13.0.5, WindowSmash's finding): the Pia result and where it was reported.

test_patches.py knew no OBS_OPTIONAL table and failed on the Smash profile
since the login gate; it reads those rows like OBS now, and the profile's
BINDING rows name a purpose the list has.

Upstream-Status: fork-only (online play is out of nxnative's scope)
Reason: Nextendo online play for Super Smash Bros. Ultimate
Issue: yewsiff/NX2Apple (no tracker: issues are disabled on this fork)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
